<!-- Source: https://github.com/TFH-Web/my-tfh-org/blob/master/Other/Forms/what-we-do-serve-team-interest-form/serve-team-picker.lava -->
{% comment %}
  =============================================================
  Serve Team Signup — Step 1: Team Picker (Lava Application Page)
  =============================================================
  Sits between the existing Campus Picker (page 1092) and the existing
  native Workflow form (WF 1091, form 1567).

  Flow:
    Welcome HTML block --> Campus Picker (1092) --> THIS PAGE --> WF 1091 form

  Campus Picker appends ?CampusId=[int] to whatever returnurl it was given
  (see its own Lava: Workflow | Attribute:'Campus1','Id'). This page reads
  that same CampusId, uses it to pull only the teams active for that
  campus, and on submit forwards to the existing form with CampusId, Team
  (comma-separated Connection Opportunity **Ids**, not Guids), and
  Source=picker all appended — mirroring Campus Picker's own "does the URL
  already have a ?" append logic.

  Source=picker exists because this page is NOT a workflow form itself —
  there's no workflow action or attribute running here, just this page's
  own JS building a redirect URL. So this is the only place that can flag
  "this person came through the picker" for the native form to consume.
  On the receiving end, WF 1091 needs a new/extended action that reads
  Source via PageParameter and stores it as a workflow attribute, which
  Form 1567's Header/PreHtml Lava then checks to decide whether to hide
  the Campus + Serving Teams of Interest fields. See build plan Step 2
  for the full reasoning.

  CONFIRMED WORKING: the destination form's "Set Serve Team Of Interest"
  Lava action was patched to split `Team` on comma and look up each Id
  individually, joining the resulting Guids back together to populate
  ServingTeamsofInterest -- tested with Team=77,6&CampusId=3, which
  correctly pre-checks Audio + Baptism (full story and the patched Lava in
  serve-sunday_team-signup-build-plan.md, Step 1).

  This page itself is live-tested too: card grid renders, campus filtering
  works, selection and Clear selection both work, and Next correctly
  redirects into the native form with CampusId + Team appended. One bug
  surfaced along the way -- loading with no CampusId in the URL left it
  genuinely blank (not 0), breaking the {% sql %} block's DECLARE
  statement. Fixed by guarding against 0, '', and null before defaulting to
  campus 2 (general write-up in learnings/rock-lava-web-quirks.md, "Blank
  Lava-Interpolated Variables Break {% sql %} Blocks").

  Team=[id],[id] pre-selection: if a Team param arrives on THIS page (not
  just the destination form), matching cards are pre-selected on load --
  counts toward the 3, still fully editable. Only Ids that match an actual
  card for the current campus are honored, capped at maxSelections, so a
  stale or out-of-campus Id in a link can't inflate the count. This is the
  "I already know I'm signing up for this one" case (e.g. visited a booth),
  NOT Phase 2's featured-3 concept -- those are different UI behaviors.

  RESOLVED since the above was written: Source flag + Visibility Rules hide
  Campus/ServingTeamsofInterest correctly on the native form (see build plan
  Step 2); native form's checkbox grey-out-on-load bug is fixed (see
  learnings/rock-lava-web-quirks.md); internal testing via the admin-gated
  test button on the live Welcome block is underway.

  Phase 2 -- Featured + See More (Sept 13): FeaturedTeam=[id],[id] marks
  cards as featured (data-featured="true" set per-card by the Lava loop,
  padded-comma-contains check against featuredIdsPadded so "7" doesn't
  false-match inside "77"). At page load, JS moves any featured cards into
  their own "Featured" section (badge via .serve-card--featured, capped at
  maxSelections defensively) and collapses the remainder behind a "See
  More" toggle. No FeaturedTeam param means no card ever gets
  data-featured="true", so the page renders exactly as it did in Phase 1,
  a single flat grid, no split. Featured and "See More" are exclusive (a
  team never appears in both), avoiding any dual-location selection-sync
  problem. Selection/limit logic (updateState, click handlers) needed zero
  changes for this: cards is a static NodeList captured before any of this
  runs, and moving a card via appendChild doesn't drop its listeners or
  invalidate that reference.

  -------------------------------------------------------------
  STYLING — 2026-08-19: this page has NO style block anymore.
  -------------------------------------------------------------
  Every rule moved into the theme, at Admin -> CMS -> Themes -> MyTFH-2021
  -> Theme Styler -> CSS Overrides, tracked in this repo as
  theme/Styles/_css-overrides.less **section 23. Serve Team Picker**.

  Why it changed, not just where it moved: the old inline styles were
  written against var(--tfh-*, ...) custom properties that are not defined
  anywhere on this site, so every one of them was silently falling back to
  its second argument -- and those fallbacks were the **rock.tfh.org
  internal** design system (#36454f brand, 10px radii, 1px #eee borders,
  hover box-shadows). That is the wrong site's look. my.tfh.org is the
  public system: black ink, #F1F1F1 panels, 20px radii, Neue Haas Grotesk,
  and no shadows anywhere.

  The palette now lives once, in section 0.1 of that same file, as the
  shared @mytfh-* tokens. Section 22 (public sign-up pages) aliases them
  and section 23 uses them directly, so this page and /signups cannot drift
  apart. Class names are feature-named with no vendor prefix, per this
  repo's convention -- `serve-`, not `tfh-`.

  Do not reintroduce a style block here. Add to section 23 instead.

  NOTE — why tag examples below are written with spaced angle brackets
  (`< p >< br >< /p >`): Rock's HTML Content editor validates the RAW text
  of the block and does not understand Lava comments, so a literal `style`
  or `script` tag written inside a Lava comment block still counts toward
  its open/close tally. (For the same reason this sentence says "a Lava
  comment block" in words: spelling that tag out literally here would put a
  second opener inside this very comment, and if Fluid's parser counts
  nesting it would treat the one closing tag below as the inner close and
  swallow the rest of the file -- a blank page, not an error message.) An earlier draft of this comment spelled the style tag
  out properly and Rock refused the paste with "End tag ... was not found",
  because it had counted two openers in prose and no closer anywhere.

  -------------------------------------------------------------
  PERFORMANCE — 2026-08-19, sized for ~6,000 visitors on a Sunday
  -------------------------------------------------------------
  Baseline measured in an incognito window (a first pass was polluted by
  browser extensions and by being logged in as admin, which loads Rock's
  Obsidian admin bundle that public visitors never see): 40 requests,
  2.2 MB transferred, DOMContentLoaded 680 ms, Load 2.20 s.

  Where that went: the 11 team photos were 880 kB, 40% of the page, each
  taking 0.3-1.55s of Rock's time through GetImage.ashx. That is the
  dominant cost, and not because of bytes -- 11 handler hits per visitor
  is 66,000 requests against the app pool across the morning, eleven times
  what the page itself generates.

  Two fixes are in the card markup below, both commented where they live:
  w=600&quality=80 on the image URL, and lazy loading for everything past
  the first row. The second one is why the photo is a real img element
  instead of a CSS background-image -- backgrounds cannot be natively
  lazy-loaded.

  Still outstanding, and both bigger than anything in this file:
  - RESOLVED 2026-08-20: the 754 ms "307" seen in DevTools was an artifact
    of typing the address, which reaches the server over http and takes a
    real 301 plus a whole second connection (2 conns vs 1, measured). It is
    NOT a visitor-facing cost here: the QR code and NFC tags both carry the
    full https URL, so no redirect happens. Worth knowing if anyone ever
    prints a bare domain -- there is no HSTS header on either hostname.
  - RegisterPageInteraction is a database write per page view, and was
    measured at 1.52s. It is async so it does not block rendering, but it
    is 6,000 extra writes during the spike.

  Whatever caching gets added, remember every cache is cold at 8:00 AM --
  block output, persisted datasets, and especially the resized image
  derivatives, which are generated on first request. Warm them the day
  before by loading the page once per campus id, or the first arrivals pay
  the full uncached cost during the exact peak being optimised for.

  STILL TO DO — see the build plan (currently at Step 9/10):
  1. Confirm Step 9's Featured/See More UI matches expectations once
     Bethany reviews it, then move to Step 10 (re-test with a real
     FeaturedTeam link).
  2. Two smaller loose ends from Phase 1, still open: verify the icon
     fallback class (`fa fa-users`) matches whatever Font Awesome version
     is in use (v6 syntax is `fa-solid fa-users`), and decide what a blank
     Summary should look like on a card (accept the sparse look, or add
     fallback text). The same question applies to `fa fa-check` on the
     selection tick and `fa fa-chevron-down` on See More.
  3. Do not point the real "Get Started" button at this page until Task
     #5's internal review is fully signed off by everyone who needs to
     weigh in.
  =============================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% assign campusIdRaw = 'Global' | PageParameter:'CampusId' %}
{% assign campusId = campusIdRaw | AsInteger %}
{% if campusId == 0 or campusId == '' or campusId == null %}{% assign campusId = 2 %}{% endif %}
{% assign destinationUrl = 'https://my.tfh.org/serveteam/what-we-do/form' %}
{% assign maxSelections = 3 %}
{% assign teamParamRaw = 'Global' | PageParameter:'Team' %}
{% assign featuredParamRaw = 'Global' | PageParameter:'FeaturedTeam' %}
{% assign featuredIdsPadded = ',' | Append:featuredParamRaw | Append:',' %}

{% sql return:'teams' %}
    DECLARE @CampusId INT = {{ campusId }}

    SELECT
        CO.[Id]
        , CO.[Name]
        , CO.[PublicName]
        , CO.[Summary]
        , CO.[Guid]
        , CO.[IconCssClass]
        , BF.[Guid] AS [PhotoGuid]

    FROM
        [ConnectionOpportunity] CO

    JOIN [ConnectionOpportunityCampus] CC ON CC.[ConnectionOpportunityId] = CO.[Id]
    LEFT JOIN [Attribute] A ON A.[EntityTypeQualifierValue] = CO.[ConnectionTypeId] AND CO.[ConnectionTypeId] = 1 AND A.[Id] = 44230
    LEFT JOIN [AttributeValue] AV ON AV.[AttributeId] = A.[Id] AND AV.[EntityId] = CO.[Id]
    LEFT JOIN [BinaryFile] BF ON BF.[Id] = CO.[PhotoId]

    WHERE CO.[IsActive] = 1
    AND CC.[CampusId] = @CampusId
    AND ( (CO.[ConnectionTypeId] = 1 AND AV.[Value] = 'True') OR CO.[Id] = 52 )

    ORDER BY CO.[Name]
{% endsql %}

{%- comment -%}
  No outer padding or max-width on this wrapper. Rock already pads the block,
  and constraining the width here made the content narrower than the page title
  above it. Width belongs at the page-layout level so everything on the page
  agrees -- the same call section 22 documents for /signups.

  mb-5 is the deliberate exception, kept at Tim's call on 2026-08-19: this is
  the last block on the page and it otherwise sits too close to the footer.
  It is the theme's own utility (margin-bottom: 3rem) rather than a margin
  declared in section 23, so the spacing stays adjustable from the block
  markup without a theme recompile.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="serve mb-5">

    <div class="serve__step">Step 1 of 2</div>
    <h1 class="serve__title">Find Your Place To Serve</h1>
    <p class="serve__intro">Choose the teams you're interested in joining (up to {{ maxSelections }}), then continue to your contact info.</p>

    <div class="serve__bar">
        <span class="serve__count" id="serveSelectionCount" aria-live="polite">0 of {{ maxSelections }} selected</span>
        <button type="button" class="serve__clear" id="serveClearSelection">Clear selection</button>
    </div>

    <div class="serve__section serve-hide" id="serveFeaturedSection">
        <div class="serve__sectionlabel">Featured</div>
        <div class="serve__grid" id="serveFeaturedGrid"></div>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="serve__more serve-hide" id="serveMoreToggle" aria-expanded="false">
        <span id="serveMoreLabel">See More</span> <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
    </button>

    <div class="serve__grid" id="serveTeamGrid">
        {% for team in teams %}
            {% assign teamIdPadded = ',' | Append:team.Id | Append:',' %}
            {% assign isFeatured = false %}
            {% if featuredIdsPadded contains teamIdPadded %}{% assign isFeatured = true %}{% endif %}
            {%- comment -%}
              Summary is authored in Rock's HTML editor and can arrive carrying
              trailing empty paragraphs. Verified against prod 2026-08-19: of
              the 11 teams on campus 2, exactly one -- Baptism (Id 6) -- ends
              with `< /p >< p >< br >< /p >< p >< br >< /p >`. Those two empty paragraphs
              rendered as real line boxes at the bottom of what was already the
              tallest card in the row, and because CSS grid rows size to their
              tallest item, that one card's junk stretched every other card
              beside it. See _temporary-files/serve-team-summary-trailing-markup.sql.

              This MUST be fixed here rather than in CSS: `< p >< br >< /p >`
              is not :empty -- it has a br child -- so no selector can
              collapse it.

              The pattern is stripped rather than the markup being flattened
              with StripHtml, because two summaries carry inline formatting
              worth keeping: Guest Services bolds its list of sub-teams, and
              Video & Lighting uses a mid-sentence &nbsp;. The alternation has
              no backslashes in it on purpose -- Fluid rejects invalid escape
              sequences inside string literals, so `\s` would fail to parse.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% assign teamDesc = team.Summary | RegExReplace:'(<p>(<br>|<br/>|<br />|&nbsp;| )*</p>)+$','' %}
            <div class="serve-card"
                 role="button"
                 tabindex="0"
                 aria-pressed="false"
                 data-id="{{ team.Id }}"
                 data-guid="{{ team.Guid }}"
                 data-name="{{ team.PublicName | Default:team.Name }}"
                 data-featured="{{ isFeatured }}">
                <span class="serve-card__tick" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa fa-check"></i></span>
                {%- comment -%}
                  The first row stays eager, everything after it is lazy. At
                  >=768px the grid is three across, so cards 1-3 are the only
                  ones reliably above the fold; lazy-loading those would defer
                  the largest thing on screen and push LCP out rather than
                  pulling it in.

                  This is deliberately an approximation. The Featured/See More
                  JS can reorder cards after load, and on a phone the grid is
                  one column so even card 2 is below the fold. Loop position is
                  the only signal available at render time, and being wrong
                  costs a slightly early or slightly late fetch -- not a broken
                  page -- so it is not worth more machinery than this.

                  The test is written as "> 3" rather than the other way round
                  on purpose: same result, but it keeps a bare < out of the
                  block. Rock's HTML editor scans the raw text and has already
                  rejected one paste of this file over a tag it thought it saw
                  in prose -- no reason to hand it another angle bracket to
                  consider.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {% assign imgLoading = 'eager' %}
                {% if forloop.index > 3 %}{% assign imgLoading = 'lazy' %}{% endif %}
                <div class="serve-card__media">
                    {% if team.PhotoGuid and team.PhotoGuid != '' %}
                        {%- comment -%}
                          w=600 covers the ~287px card at 2x, and quality=80
                          is required alongside it -- NOT optional.

                          Rock's manual documents w / h as the resize params
                          ("Working With Images", Designing and Building
                          Websites Using Rock). maxwidth / maxheight also work,
                          since GetImage sits on the ImageResizer library, but
                          they are not in Rock's docs -- w is used here so the
                          URL matches what is documented. Verified byte- and
                          pixel-identical on prod 2026-08-20:
                          w=600&quality=80 and maxwidth=600&quality=80 both
                          returned 34 kB at 600x603 for the same file.

                          WHY quality IS MANDATORY: the manual states the
                          default is 90, and "Quality can often be set much
                          lower than the default." Resizing alone therefore
                          RE-ENCODES AT 90, which for photos stored below that
                          makes the resized copy BIGGER than the original.
                          Measured across all 11 campus-2 photos 2026-08-19:

                            original               856 kB
                            resize only            614 kB  (-28%, 5 got BIGGER)
                            resize + quality=80    431 kB  (-49%, none bigger)

                          60 gives another ~10 kB per image and the manual
                          encourages going lower, but 80 was kept as the safe
                          setting for photographs of faces.

                          Do NOT add format=webp. The manual lists the valid
                          options as jpg, png and gif only, and passing webp
                          makes GetImage silently ignore the resize entirely
                          and return the full original -- with a 200, so it
                          fails invisibly.

                          Do NOT add disableoptimizations=true here. It turns
                          Rock's resizing OFF so a CDN can do it instead. It
                          only becomes relevant if Cloudflare Polish or Image
                          Resizing is ever enabled, at which point the manual
                          warns Rock and the CDN "will often conflict causing
                          both Rock and the CDN to resize and optimize the
                          file" -- and then these w/quality params must come
                          off at the same time.

                          Server-side the derivative IS cached: first request
                          for a given size took 1.34s, subsequent ones ~0.45s.
                          That is why these URLs need warming before a spike --
                          see the PERFORMANCE note in the header comment.

                          The separator is a bare ampersand rather than an
                          entity because that is what Rock's own core templates
                          and this site's existing logo URL use; it is the form
                          proven to survive the HTML editor here.

                          alt is intentionally empty. The team name is rendered
                          immediately below in serve-card__name, inside the same
                          control, so descriptive alt text would just read the
                          name out twice to a screen reader. The photo is
                          decorative in this context.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        <img src="/GetImage.ashx?Guid={{ team.PhotoGuid }}&w=600&quality=80"
                             alt=""
                             loading="{{ imgLoading }}"
                             decoding="async">
                    {% else %}
                        <i class="{{ team.IconCssClass | Default:'fa fa-users' }}"></i>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
                <div class="serve-card__body">
                    <div class="serve-card__name">{{ team.PublicName | Default:team.Name }}</div>
                    <div class="serve-card__desc">{{ teamDesc }}</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="serve__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="serveNextBtn" disabled>Next</button>
    </div>

</div>

<script>
(function () {
    var maxSelections = {{ maxSelections }};
    var campusId = '{{ campusId }}';
    var destinationUrl = '{{ destinationUrl }}';
    var preselectedTeams = '{{ teamParamRaw }}';
    var selected = [];

    var grid = document.getElementById('serveTeamGrid');
    var cards = grid.querySelectorAll('.serve-card');
    var countLabel = document.getElementById('serveSelectionCount');
    var nextBtn = document.getElementById('serveNextBtn');
    var clearBtn = document.getElementById('serveClearSelection');

    // Restore prior selection when arriving with ?Team=, e.g. "I visited a
    // booth and already know I'm signing up for this one." Only teams that
    // actually appear as cards for this campus get pre-selected, and the
    // list is capped at maxSelections, so a stale or out-of-campus Id in
    // the link can't inflate the count or leave it out of sync with what's
    // visually shown.
    if (preselectedTeams) {
        var cardIds = [];
        cards.forEach(function (card) { cardIds.push(card.getAttribute('data-id')); });

        selected = preselectedTeams.split(',')
            .map(function (id) { return id.trim(); })
            .filter(function (id) { return id !== '' && cardIds.indexOf(id) > -1; })
            .slice(0, maxSelections);
    }

    // Phase 2: split off featured cards (marked via data-featured by the Lava
    // loop above) into their own "Featured" section, with the remainder
    // collapsed under a "See More" toggle. cards is a static NodeList
    // captured before this runs, and moving a node via appendChild doesn't
    // remove its event listeners or invalidate that reference, so no
    // changes are needed to updateState() or the click handlers below,
    // they keep working across both containers automatically. If no
    // FeaturedTeam param is present, no card ever gets data-featured="true",
    // so this block finds nothing to move and the page renders exactly as
    // it did before Phase 2, a single flat grid.
    var featuredSection = document.getElementById('serveFeaturedSection');
    var featuredGrid = document.getElementById('serveFeaturedGrid');
    var moreToggle = document.getElementById('serveMoreToggle');
    var moreLabel = document.getElementById('serveMoreLabel');
    var moreIcon = moreToggle.querySelector('i');

    var featuredCards = Array.prototype.filter.call(cards, function (card) {
        return card.getAttribute('data-featured') === 'true';
    }).slice(0, maxSelections); // defensive cap in case more than 3 get configured by mistake

    if (featuredCards.length > 0) {
        featuredCards.forEach(function (card) {
            card.classList.add('serve-card--featured');
            featuredGrid.appendChild(card);
        });

        featuredSection.classList.remove('serve-hide');
        moreToggle.classList.remove('serve-hide');
        grid.classList.add('serve-hide');

        moreToggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
            var isCollapsed = grid.classList.contains('serve-hide');
            grid.classList.toggle('serve-hide', !isCollapsed);
            moreToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isCollapsed ? 'true' : 'false');
            moreLabel.textContent = isCollapsed ? 'See Less' : 'See More';
            moreIcon.classList.toggle('fa-chevron-down', !isCollapsed);
            moreIcon.classList.toggle('fa-chevron-up', isCollapsed);
        });
    }

    function updateState() {
        var atLimit = selected.length >= maxSelections;

        countLabel.textContent = selected.length + ' of ' + maxSelections + ' selected';
        nextBtn.disabled = selected.length === 0;

        cards.forEach(function (card) {
            var id = card.getAttribute('data-id');
            var isSelected = selected.indexOf(id) > -1;
            var isDisabled = !isSelected && atLimit;

            card.classList.toggle('serve-card--selected', isSelected);
            card.classList.toggle('serve-card--disabled', isDisabled);
            card.setAttribute('aria-pressed', isSelected ? 'true' : 'false');

            // pointer-events:none stops the mouse but not the keyboard, so a
            // card that's out of reach has to leave the tab order too.
            card.setAttribute('aria-disabled', isDisabled ? 'true' : 'false');
            card.tabIndex = isDisabled ? -1 : 0;
        });
    }

    function toggleCard(card) {
        if (card.getAttribute('aria-disabled') === 'true') { return; }

        var id = card.getAttribute('data-id');
        var idx = selected.indexOf(id);

        if (idx > -1) {
            selected.splice(idx, 1);
        } else if (selected.length < maxSelections) {
            selected.push(id);
        }
        updateState();
    }

    cards.forEach(function (card) {
        card.addEventListener('click', function () {
            toggleCard(card);
        });

        // role="button" is a promise that Enter and Space activate it.
        card.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
            if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'Spacebar') {
                e.preventDefault();
                toggleCard(card);
            }
        });
    });

    clearBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        selected = [];
        updateState();
    });

    nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (selected.length === 0) { return; }

        var separator = destinationUrl.indexOf('?') > -1 ? '&' : '?';
        var url = destinationUrl + separator
            + 'CampusId=' + encodeURIComponent(campusId)
            + '&Team=' + encodeURIComponent(selected.join(','))
            + '&Source=picker';

        window.location.href = url;
    });

    updateState();
})();
</script>
